      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bo'ness"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town of Bo'ness has served as a filming location for the TV series Outlander and Mel Gibson's production of Hamlet.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://bonet.org.uk/visit/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Kinneil House, located to the west of Bo'ness, was mentioned by Bede and is now cared for by Historic Scotland.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bo'ness"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Bo'ness continues to celebrate the Children's Fair Festival, which is covered by the local radio station Valley FM.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bo'ness"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Glebe Park in the town centre features a bandstand constructed in 1902 by the Walter McFarlane and Company Saracen Foundry.",
